BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a sa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (    cred well, but the Elder's Well held a mysterious power: any water poured into it would trip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (    le before flowing underground to the Sister's Well in the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (  The villages began a ritual. Each moon, the Elder would carry water from their well across the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (     valley. Whatever amount they chose to pour into the sacred well would multiply threefold by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (     the time it reached the Sister village. The Sister would then decide how much to carry back) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (     in gratitude.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (  At first, both villages were cautious, sharing only droplets. But as trust grew, the Elder pou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (    red more generously, and the Sister returned abundantly. Both villages flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (  Yet the mountains sometimes whispered false numbers-what one village poured was not always wha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (    t the other heard. Wise villagers learned to look past these stone-echoes, judging intention) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    s over precise measurements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  The myth teaches: *True abundance flows from the courage to give first, the wisdom to return f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    airly, and the grace to forgive the mountain's occasional lies.* When both villages trusted ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    in this pattern, neither well ran dry, and the valley bloomed eternal.) Tj ET
