BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (     sacred spring, but the water barely sustained them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  One day, a wanderer discovered a secret: water poured from one spring into the valley's hidden) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     depths would emerge threefold from the other spring. But the giver would lose their water, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    trusting the receiver to share the bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  The villages faced a choice. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  The first village poured generously, watching their spring run low. The second village receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    d abundance - water multiplied beyond measure. They could keep it all, or honor the gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  Wisely, they returned more than was given. The first village's spring overflowed with the retu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    rned water. Seeing this, they gave again, even more generously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  With each exchange, both springs grew stronger, until the valley bloomed green and both villag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    es prospered beyond imagination.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  But when greed entered one village's heart - when they kept everything or gave nothing - both ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    springs weakened, and the valley returned to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
