BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possess) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        ed a sacred spring, but the water barely sustained them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      One day, a wanderer discovered a secret: water poured from one spring into the valley's hi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        dden depths would emerge threefold from the other spring. But the giver would lose their) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (         water, trusting the receiver to share the bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The villages faced a choice. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      The first village poured generously, watching their spring run low. The second village rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        eived abundance - water multiplied beyond measure. They could keep it all, or honor the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        gift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      Wisely, they returned more than was given. The first village's spring overflowed with the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        returned water. Seeing this, they gave again, even more generously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      With each exchange, both springs grew stronger, until the valley bloomed green and both vi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        llages prospered beyond imagination.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      But when greed entered one village's heart - when they kept everything or gave nothing - b) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        oth springs weakened, and the valley returned to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      The elders taught: *The springs remember every gift and every betrayal. Trust multiplies a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        bundance, but broken faith withers all.*) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    reasoning:) Tj ET
