BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        a sacred well, but the Elder's Well held a mysterious power: any water poured into it wo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        uld triple before flowing underground to the Sister's Well in the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      The villages began a ritual. Each moon, the Elder would carry water from their well across) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         the valley. Whatever amount they chose to pour into the sacred well would multiply thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        efold by the time it reached the Sister village. The Sister would then decide how much t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        o carry back in gratitude.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      At first, both villages were cautious, sharing only droplets. But as trust grew, the Elder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         poured more generously, and the Sister returned abundantly. Both villages flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      Yet the mountains sometimes whispered false numbers-what one village poured was not always) Tj ET
