BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        a sacred well, but the Elder's Well held a mysterious power: any water poured into it wo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        uld triple before flowing underground to the Sister's Well in the other village.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      The villages began a ritual. Each moon, the Elder would carry water from their well across) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         the valley. Whatever amount they chose to pour into the sacred well would multiply thre) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        efold by the time it reached the Sister village. The Sister would then decide how much t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        o carry back in gratitude.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      At first, both villages were cautious, sharing only droplets. But as trust grew, the Elder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (         poured more generously, and the Sister returned abundantly. Both villages flourished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
